<%# Full page rendered by AlertRulesController#new (see
    app/controllers/alert_rules_controller.rb) — shown when visiting GET
    /alert_rules/new. The controller has already built a blank, unsaved
    `AlertRule.new` object into `@alert_rule`, so every field in the shared
    form partial below starts empty (or at its model default) rather than
    erroring out on a missing record. %>
<div class="mb-6">
  <%# "mb-6" adds margin below this heading block, before the form card. %>
  <%# "text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-400" is plain styling — large, bold,
      green-accented heading text. Unlike edit.html.erb's heading, this one
      has no `<%= % >` interpolation since there's no existing record name
      to display yet — it's just static text. %>
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-400">New Alert Rule</h1>
</div>
<%# "card" is this app's custom boxed/panel styling class; "max-w-2xl" caps
    the box's maximum width so the form doesn't stretch too wide on large
    screens. %>
<div class="card max-w-2xl">
  <%# `render "form", alert_rule: @alert_rule` pulls in the shared partial
      at app/views/alert_rules/_form.html.erb (the leading underscore in
      that filename marks it as a partial — a reusable snippet, not a full
      page of its own — and `render "form"` finds it by that naming
      convention). `alert_rule: @alert_rule` passes this page's blank,
      unsaved record into the partial as a local variable named
      `alert_rule`, which the partial's form fields read from to decide
      what to pre-fill (nothing, here) and where the form submits to.
      Because `@alert_rule.new_record?` is true for this blank record, the
      shared partial automatically points its <form> at the "create" action
      and labels its submit button "Create Alert Rule" — see the comments
      in _form.html.erb for exactly how that happens. This is the SAME
      partial app/views/alert_rules/edit.html.erb also renders, so the new
      and edit forms share one single source of truth for their fields. %>
  <%= render "form", alert_rule: @alert_rule %>
</div>
